.newspapers.com","hostname":"newspapers.com","summary":"Searchable archive of historical US newspapers.","detail":"Largest newspaper archive in the US — 900M+ newspaper pages from 1700s to 2000s. Search for a person's name across historical papers. Great for finding obituaries, arrest records, court notices, and historical mentions.","howTo":["Enter the name or event to search","Filter by date range and state/city","Click results to view the original newspaper page","Save clippings to your account"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","freemium"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["news"],"agentTool":"osint.newspapers-com"},{"id":"google-advanced-search","name":"Google Advanced Search","url":"https://www.google.com/advanced_search","hostname":"google.com","summary":"GUI for building complex Google search queries without remembering syntax.","detail":"Google's advanced search UI. Input fields for all words, exact phrases, any words, excluded words, language, region, site, filetype, and date range. No need to remember operator syntax.","howTo":["Fill in the relevant fields","Click 'Advanced Search'","Note the resulting URL — it shows the raw Google query for reuse","Bookmark effective queries for future reference"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["search_engines"],"agentTool":"osint.google-advanced-search"},{"id":"yandex","name":"Yandex","url":"https://yandex.com","hostname":"yandex.com","summary":"Russian search engine — superior for CIS-region content and reverse image search.","detail":"Yandex indexes Russian-language content far more comprehensively than Google. Its reverse image search is more powerful than Google's, especially for faces and Eastern European content.","howTo":["Use yandex.com for English search or yandex.ru for Russian","Images: yandex.com/images — camera icon for reverse image search","Use Cyrillic transliteration for Russian name searches","Yandex often surfaces VK profiles, Russian news, and forum posts that Google misses"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["search_engines"],"agentTool":"osint.yandex"},{"id":"searx","name":"Searx","url":"https://searx.info","hostname":"searx.info","summary":"Open-source, self-hostable meta search engine — aggregates results without tracking.","detail":"Privacy-respecting meta search engine. Aggregates results from Google, Bing, DuckDuckGo, and others without storing your searches or creating a search profile. Self-hostable for full control.","howTo":["Use the public instance or self-host","Select which engines to include in settings","No tracking, no filter bubble","Results aggregate across multiple engines in one view"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["search_engines"],"agentTool":"osint.searx"},{"id":"grep-app-code-search","name":"Grep.app (Code Search)","url":"https://grep.app","hostname":"grep.app","summary":"Regex search across 500,000 public GitHub repositories.","detail":"Fast code search with full regex support. Essential for finding exposed credentials, API keys, and sensitive data committed to public GitHub repositories.","howTo":["Enter a keyword or regex pattern","Filter by programming language","Review matching code with context","Click through to the file in GitHub for full context"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["search_engines"],"agentTool":"osint.grep-app-code-search"},{"id":"million-short","name":"Million Short","url":"https://millionshort.com","hostname":"millionshort.com","summary":"Removes the top N websites from results — surfaces the hidden web.","detail":"A search engine that removes the top N results from its results (configurable: top 100 to top 1M sites). Reveals content that would normally be buried under high-authority sites. Good for finding obscure mentions.","howTo":["Enter your search term","Select how many top sites to remove (start with top 100)","Review results that normally would never surface","Increase the removal count to dig deeper"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["search_engines"],"agentTool":"osint.million-short"},{"id":"google-scholar","name":"Google Scholar","url":"https://scholar.google.com","hostname":"scholar.google.com","summary":"Academic literature search — patents, theses, and peer-reviewed papers.","detail":"Searches academic papers, patents, theses, and court opinions. Useful for finding technical research, expert witnesses, and academic publications by a subject. Also reveals institutional affiliations.","howTo":["Search by author name, keyword, or institution","Use 'Cited by' to find papers that reference a specific work","Alert: set up Scholar alerts for author names to track new publications","Advanced: author:LastName to search by author name"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["search_engines"],"agentTool":"osint.google-scholar"},{"id":"bevigil","name":"BeVigil","url":"https://bevigil.com","hostname":"bevigil.com","summary":"Searches for secrets inside mobile app packages — endpoints, keys, and config.","detail":"Security search engine that analyzes mobile apps and extracts exposed API endpoints, hardcoded credentials, S3 bucket names, and other sensitive data from app code. Useful for finding backend infrastructure.","howTo":["Search by app name, domain, or endpoint pattern","Review extracted endpoints and parameters","Look for internal domain names and API endpoints","Hardcoded credentials sometimes appear in app decompilation results"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","freemium"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["search_engines"],"agentTool":"osint.bevigil"},{"id":"sploitus","name":"Sploitus","url":"https://sploitus.com","hostname":"sploitus.com","summary":"Exploit and vulnerability search engine — aggregates ExploitDB, GitHub, and more.","detail":"Searches for public exploits and vulnerabilities across ExploitDB, GitHub, Packet Storm, and other sources. Useful for identifying whether a target's known software versions have public exploits.","howTo":["Enter CVE number, software name, or product version","Review exploits from multiple sources","Check the GitHub tab for proof-of-concept code","Cross-reference with VirusTotal if downloading any files"],"proTip":null,"alternatives":[],"tags":["web","free"],"installCommand":null,"categoryIds":["search_engines"],"agentTool":"osint.sploitus"}]}